      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FLYING GENTRY (4) missed the placings when resuming at Pakenham Synthetic two runs back then improved last start but found one better over 1429m at Sale, beaten 2.5 lengths after being prominent at the corner. Beautifully placed and is sure to play a major role. CABLE BOY (1) got home by 0.6 lengths on dirt at Broome two starts ago. Disappointed in another run on dirt last time at Broome over 1300m when 5.5 lengths from the winner in fourth. Looks a strong chance to find winning form here. THROW AT DA STUMPS (2) missed the placings two runs back then was always well out of his ground last start when eighth over 1300m at Darwin. Has started two times at this course and distance and is yet to miss the placings. Finds a nice race and can take this out. PREDICTING (6) returned from a spell three-and-a-half weeks ago when he was in contention on the corner before being beaten 2.25 lengths into sixth over 1100m at Darwin. Fitter and sure to run well. THE FINAL WORD (3) is next.",
